  "id": "bhavai",
  "name": "Bhavai (Gujarati folk-theatre music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bhavai is the folk theatre of northern Gujarat, performed by hereditary troupes of the Targala (Nayak) community, who trace it to the fourteenth-century Asait Thakar. A troupe plays a sequence of short plays (vesh) in the village square through the night, mixing song, dance and comic dialogue. Its signature sound is the bhungal, a long copper trumpet, heard with pakhawaj, tabla and manjira cymbals; the karna card stands in for the bhungal.",
